    "narrative": "The slate for Ghost Ride the WHIP is anchored by **Corbin Carroll** (85.94), who draws an elite matchup against Lowder; with a favorable park and a significant SP skill advantage, **Corbin Carroll** is our primary source of upside today. **Vinnie Pasquantino** (71.83) and **Gabriel Moreno** (71.17) also profile as high-efficiency starts, both benefiting from soft matchups against Burrows and Lowder, respectively. **James Wood** (64.15) remains a priority play despite facing a tougher arm in Castillo; his elite xwOBA and top-of-the-order usage keep his floor high even when the opposing SP isn't crumbling. **Josh Naylor** (64.79) also maintains a strong profile, serving as a reliable engine for RBI and R production against Cavalli.\n\nWe are monitoring several \"Lineup Pending\" statuses, most notably **Max Muncy** (59.63) and **Kyle Karros** (58.85), whose projections are buoyed by favorable matchups against Freeland and Estes, respectively. **Jose Caballero** (46.99) carries a volatile profile today; while his stolen base potential is always a factor, the brutal 13% drag from his platoon split against Gausman puts him near the bottom of our active starters. The most difficult bench decision involved **Austin Riley** (44.90), who barely missed the cut. Despite his name value, a poor park factor and a difficult matchup against Manaea resulted in a lower efficiency score than the rest of our utility-heavy roster. \n\nRisk management remains paramount today, particularly for **Brice Turang** (54.45) and **Seiya Suzuki** (44.52). **Brice Turang** is hampered by facing Nola and a restrictive catcher matchup that suppresses his base-stealing upside, while **Seiya Suzuki** is battling a significant SP skill disadvantage. We\u2019ve benched **Travis Bazzana** (32.78) entirely, as facing a pitcher of Skubal\u2019s caliber makes him a liability for our daily game caps. Ensure all notifications are active for **Max Muncy**, **Brice Turang**, **Kyle Karros**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, and **Seiya Suzuki** as official lineups drop; any further shift in their batting order could necessitate a quick pivot to our bench options.",
